1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,145
Danny Reyes hummed when he was nervous.

2
00:00:03,195 --> 00:00:08,158
And he was always a little nervous, so he was
always humming.

3
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:10,989
Badly. Off-key and a half-beat behind.

4
00:00:11,039 --> 00:00:17,820
The same three songs on a loop, inside a helmet
that smelled like rain and fried chicken.

5
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:23,196
He was twenty-nine, and by his own count, had
delivered eleven thousand meals.

6
00:00:23,246 --> 00:00:27,118
And he had never once eaten what he carried.

7
00:00:27,168 --> 00:00:31,767
He kept a list in his phone instead, titled,
Try Someday.

8
00:00:31,817 --> 00:00:36,053
The purple yam cheesecake from the place on
Mango Street.

9
00:00:36,103 --> 00:00:41,066
The spicy ramen that made a customer cry
laughing at the door.

10
00:00:41,116 --> 00:00:45,351
The dumplings that arrived so hot, the bag
fogged up.

11
00:00:45,401 --> 00:00:53,272
He read the list at red lights, like a man
studying a map to a country he hoped to visit.

12
00:00:53,322 --> 00:00:56,467
But someday had another meaning. Mia's
tuition.

13
00:00:56,517 --> 00:01:01,844
Nursing school, second year. The first Reyes
to ever wear a white cap.

14
00:01:01,894 --> 00:01:06,493
Danny worked from six in the morning until two
at night.

15
00:01:06,543 --> 00:01:13,687
When people asked why he never slept, he said
sleep was for people who had already made it.

16
00:01:13,737 --> 00:01:17,973
He kept every receipt in a shoebox under his
bed.

17
00:01:18,023 --> 00:01:21,895
His mother had taught him that paper protects
you.

18
00:01:21,945 --> 00:01:24,726
Just in case, he always said.

19
00:01:24,776 --> 00:01:29,012
Until Mia started saying it with him, rolling
her eyes.

20
00:01:29,062 --> 00:01:31,479
He wasn't a perfect brother.

21
00:01:31,529 --> 00:01:34,674
He forgot birthdays unless a reminder rang.

22
00:01:34,724 --> 00:01:38,596
He interrupted people. He was terrible on the
phone.

23
00:01:38,646 --> 00:01:42,518
And he'd rather send a thumbs-up than a
sentence.

24
00:01:42,568 --> 00:01:48,622
But every night, around eleven, wherever he
was, he sent his mother the same text.

25
00:01:48,672 --> 00:01:50,726
Have you eaten yet?

26
00:01:50,776 --> 00:01:55,248
She always answered with a photo of her plate.

27
00:01:55,298 --> 00:02:01,588
On the last night, it rained like the city had
decided to punish someone.

28
00:02:01,638 --> 00:02:04,419
Danny had already done fourteen orders.

29
00:02:04,469 --> 00:02:07,978
His left glove had a hole in it.

30
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:11,900
He had a fever he was calling a tickle.

31
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:14,731
Mia's graduation was in forty-one days.

32
00:02:14,781 --> 00:02:21,198
And he'd promised to sit in the front row
wearing a real collared shirt, with buttons.

33
00:02:21,248 --> 00:02:24,993
At eleven forty-seven, the delivery app
chimed.

34
00:02:25,043 --> 00:02:27,461
A cake. Chocolate. A candle.

35
00:02:27,511 --> 00:02:30,655
And a note in the order field.

36
00:02:30,705 --> 00:02:36,995
Please don't be late. It's my son's seventh
birthday, and he's been waiting up.

37
00:02:37,045 --> 00:02:39,463
Danny looked at the clock.

38
00:02:39,513 --> 00:02:41,931
He looked at the rain.

39
00:02:41,981 --> 00:02:45,126
Then he did what he always did.

40
00:02:45,176 --> 00:02:49,648
Okay, okay, he said to nobody, and pulled out.

41
00:02:49,698 --> 00:02:52,843
He took the shortcut under the overpass.

42
00:02:52,893 --> 00:02:55,142
He hummed.

43
00:02:55,192 --> 00:02:59,791
Somewhere between the second and third bar of
that familiar song,

44
00:02:59,841 --> 00:03:06,258
a truck that couldn't see the red light, or the
little yellow bike, crossed the intersection.

45
00:03:06,308 --> 00:03:09,326
There was no long moment.

46
00:03:09,376 --> 00:03:12,757
That's what people don't tell you.

47
00:03:12,807 --> 00:03:15,825
There was just the song.

48
00:03:15,875 --> 00:03:18,529
And then there wasn't.

49
00:03:18,579 --> 00:03:20,869
The cake survived.

50
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:25,028
That was the part nobody could get over.

51
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:31,858
It sat in its box on the wet road, dented on
one corner, the candle still inside.

52
00:03:31,908 --> 00:03:36,144
The little boy waited up until one in the
morning.

53
00:03:36,194 --> 00:03:39,702
His father told him the delivery was late.

54
00:03:39,752 --> 00:03:42,407
And that was true.

55
00:03:42,457 --> 00:03:45,601
Danny's phone was found in his jacket.

56
00:03:45,651 --> 00:03:48,433
The screen was cracked, but alive.

57
00:03:48,483 --> 00:03:53,446
At eleven, a message to his mother had been
sent and delivered.

58
00:03:53,496 --> 00:03:56,150
Have you eaten yet?

59
00:03:56,200 --> 00:04:01,526
She had replied at eleven oh two with a photo
of her plate.

60
00:04:01,576 --> 00:04:04,230
He never opened it.

61
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:08,152
The shoebox of receipts was still under his
bed.

62
00:04:08,202 --> 00:04:12,438
The helmet was still on the hook by the door.

63
00:04:12,488 --> 00:04:17,087
Mia hung it there every night for a week
without thinking.

64
00:04:17,137 --> 00:04:20,882
Because that was where it always went.

65
00:04:20,932 --> 00:04:26,258
On the forty-first day, Mia walked across the
stage in a white cap.

66
00:04:26,308 --> 00:04:30,544
And in the front row, there was an empty
chair.

67
00:04:30,594 --> 00:04:37,247
A collared shirt was folded over its back, the
buttons done up all the way.

68
00:04:37,297 --> 00:04:39,715
Afterward, she opened his phone.

69
00:04:39,765 --> 00:04:44,000
The one their mother couldn't bring herself to
turn off.

70
00:04:44,050 --> 00:04:46,832
And she scrolled to the list.

71
00:04:46,882 --> 00:04:49,131
Try Someday.

72
00:04:49,181 --> 00:04:51,599
She went to Mango Street.

73
00:04:51,649 --> 00:04:57,702
She ordered the purple yam cheesecake, and ate
it slowly at a table for two.

74
00:04:57,752 --> 00:05:00,043
Across from nobody.

75
00:05:00,093 --> 00:05:02,747
It was very good.

76
00:05:02,797 --> 00:05:06,178
She told him so, out loud.

77
00:05:06,228 --> 00:05:08,882
And then she hummed.

78
00:05:08,932 --> 00:05:11,950
Badly. And a half-beat behind.
